{
  "invariant": "theme-color-index-order",
  "description": "Which <a:clrScheme> slot does SpreadsheetML's theme=\"n\" index? ISO/IEC 29500 §20.1.6.2 tabulates the clrScheme child sequence as dk1, lt1, dk2, lt2, accent1..6, hlink, folHlink, and that is the order the theme part is written in — but it is not the order theme=\"n\" indexes. Excel was asked directly: twelve cells were given Interior.ThemeColor = MsoThemeColorIndex 1..12, Excel saved the file, and the emitted theme=\"n\" was read back from styles.xml; the same cells were then reopened and Interior.Color read, giving the concrete RGB Excel renders each index as. The RGB is the decisive half — the object model's own \"Dark 1\"/\"Light 1\" naming is itself swapped relative to the theme part's dk1/lt1 elements, so naming alone settles nothing.",
  "probe": ".tmp/theme-index-probe.ps1 + .tmp/theme-rgb-probe.ps1 (one-off; not a committed harness probe)",
